  "description": "Excel-VBA-style object-model wrapper around the Alibre PDM vault API. PDMApplication is the entry point. Requires Alibre Design installed on the consumer machine; it references AlibreX.dll from the Alibre install directory at runtime and does not redistribute it.",
  "id": "AlibrePDMObjectModel",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-07-25T22:47:17.073Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "vDzwLEtz8CUh5W2byrFNU2ap1LECS+VvAVaNBCKjvlMHYCSNYxzwc1PJlN4tBFgz5tTYYeIlTgiYP48ieAqAWw==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 75430,
  "published": "2026-07-25T22:44:40.82Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.2 - Fix: PDMFolder.Files and PDMFolder.Folders no longer throw NullReferenceException on a freshly created project (the COM collection is Nothing until the folder is re-fetched); they now return an empty collection. Disabled (throw NotImplementedException instead of failing badly, implementation retained): PDMFile.CheckIn and PDMFolder.UploadFiles, because the asynchronous PDM upload/check-in hangs when driven over a reused Alibre Design connection (the completion callback never reaches the STA thread); Use the Alibre PDM Browser for check-in and upload. Fix: PDMFolder.CreateFolder returned a folder whose underlying COM object was unpopulated, which made any later use of it (for example PDMFile.Move into that folder) fail with a null reference; it now re-fetches the new folder by name. PDMFile.Move also rejects an unbound destination folder with a clear message. All other operations (create/copy/move/rename/delete/lock/unlock/property get+set/revisions and the full read+browse surface) are verified against a live vault. v1.0.1 - PDMFiles.Item(name) falls back to Name/FullName enumeration when COM GetFileItemByName returns nothing.",
